  "accepted_answers": [
    "Mustafa II",
    "Malik Shah I"
  ],
  "explanation": "The question asks for the father of 'Mahmud I'. The sources present two distinct historical figures named 'Mahmud I': one as the Ottoman Sultan and another as the Sultan of the Seljuk Empire. D1S2 explicitly states that the Ottoman Sultan Mahmud I was the son of Mustafa II. D3S3, D4S1, and D5S1 identify the Seljuk Sultan Mahmud I as the son of Malik Shah I. These are separate referents, and their respective fathers are correctly identified in the sources. The candidate 'Osman III' is incorrectly presented as a father in D2S1 and conflicts with D1S3, which identifies Osman III as the younger brother of Mahmud I."
}
